==Trivia==
*The names of Eden of Evolution's stages directly relate to [[wikipedia:Charles Darwin|Charles Darwin]], the evolutionary biologist [[Sage of Selection Darvin]] is based on. [[Natural Rejection]], [[The Dogma Divide]], [[Tree of Strife]] and the Japanese name of [[The Cullosseum]] refer to [[wikipedia:Natural selection|natural selection]], [[wikipedia:Rejection of evolution by religious groups|evolution vs. creationism]], the [[wikipedia:Tree of life (biology)|tree of life]] and [[wikipedia:Survival of the fittest|survival of the fittest]] (a term actually coined by [[wikipedia:Herbert Spencer|Herbert Spencer]], but inspired by Darwin), respectively, while the others reference ''[[wikipedia:On the Origin of Species|On the Origin of Species]]'':
**[[Origin Outback]] contains "Origin", and its Japanese name, Shunoki Gen'ya (シュノキ原野), is a pun on 種の起源 ''Shu no Kigen'' ("''Origin of Species''"), with 原野 ''gen'ya'' meaning "wilderness" or "wilds".
**[[Endless Forms Most Beautiful]] is a reference to the last paragraph of ''On the Origin of Species'': "There is grandeur in this view of life, with its several powers, having been originally breathed into a few forms or into one; and that, whilst this planet has gone cycling on according to the fixed law of gravity, from so simple a beginning <u>endless forms most beautiful</u> and most wonderful have been, and are being, evolved."
**Endless Forms Most Beautiful can be seen as an "evolved" form of [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]], having a stage width of 6,000, a long-reaching boss that spawns after 10 seconds, and unlimited, alternating variants of [[Bore]] ([[Boraphim]]) and [[R.Ost]] ([[Commander Ostromeda]]) as constant threats.
*Eden of Evolution is the last [[Zero Legends]] sub-chapter to take place in a flipped and reversed Eurasia, the first being [[A Journey of Moments]].
*Eden of Evolution being the 31st Zero Legends sub-chapter and debuting Sage of Selection Darvin could potentially reference [[Galapa-Goth]], the 31st [[Stories of Legend]] sub-chapter. Galapa-Goth is named after the [[Wikipedia:Galápagos Islands|Galápagos Islands]], on which Darwin obtained evidence for his theory of evolution.

